1
00:00:02,201 --> 00:00:06,003
My brothers… I hope this letter finds you well.

2
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:09,866
I told you that I might soon ask you to join me in Ostican.

3
00:00:10,342 --> 00:00:12,224
That time has now come.

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:15,691
Let me tell you what has befallen me since we last parted.

5
00:00:15,869 --> 00:00:19,614
I have been trying to gather warriors here to help us fight the Sea Hounds.

6
00:00:19,871 --> 00:00:26,330
 I was lucky to find one very capable and brave soul who came to my help when they ambushed me in an alley.

7
00:00:26,746 --> 00:00:30,511
This warrior has a sister who was enslaved along this coast

8
00:00:30,748 --> 00:00:35,761
and agreed to join me in my hunt in the hope of learning more about her whereabouts. 

9
00:00:36,018 --> 00:00:40,139
I had planned to sail out of Ostican with our old comrade, Purig.

10
00:00:40,397 --> 00:00:43,408
I considered myself very fortunate to have found him. 

11
00:00:43,666 --> 00:00:48,956
He was a warrior, with a ship, who shared my hatred of the Sea Hounds, ready to sail with me.

12
00:00:49,352 --> 00:00:54,068
But I had misjudged him. He was instead the lowest form of traitor

13
00:00:54,166 --> 00:00:58,881
a man whose feigned camaraderie concealed a contempt for all that we value.

14
00:00:59,020 --> 00:01:04,191
The first night on the open sea, we were woken up by Purig's men holding knives to our throats.

15
00:01:04,389 --> 00:01:06,489
Purig had struck a deal with the Sea Hounds

16
00:01:06,569 --> 00:01:10,452
and he intended to hand me over to them to be tortured and killed.

17
00:01:10,590 --> 00:01:17,247
He was always ambitious, and seemed eager to win favor with what he imagined to be a new power in the north.

18
00:01:17,346 --> 00:01:20,100
“I am sorry, old friend,” he said

19
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:22,220
“But the Sea Hounds are strong and rich.

20
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:26,480
and I think you always wanted to die spitting defiance at your foes.”

21
00:01:26,579 --> 00:01:30,210
That was the last he spoke to me. His men chained us to the oars.

22
00:01:30,576 --> 00:01:32,997
The sea was calm and the weather hot.

23
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:38,613
They made us row hard and we suffered greatly as we cruised the coast, looking for merchantmen.

24
00:01:38,768 --> 00:01:43,150
Presumably, Purig wished to appear before the Sea Hounds with a prize or two in his hands

25
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:44,860
to make more of an impression.

26
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:48,750
In this way, his plan was undone by his greed.

27
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:53,100
On the third day, we came across a stubby trading knarr and gave chase.

28
00:01:53,390 --> 00:01:58,310
As we closed, the knarr's crew first started to dump their cargo and then their own selves

29
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:01,000
as the pirates were shooting them with their bows.

30
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:03,030
Eventually, we caught the knarr.

31
00:02:03,110 --> 00:02:07,950
Purig sent us as oar slaves to his prize, alongside some crew who hadn't jumped

32
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:12,220
with some pirates to guard us as he gathered up all that floating cargo.

33
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:18,500
That was a mistake. His men found some casks of wine aboard the knarr and failed to chain us properly.

34
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,608
Purig's snekkja by then was some distance away

35
00:02:21,775 --> 00:02:27,715
and we realized that if we wanted to end our miserable ordeal, we'd never get a better opportunity.

